  "slug": "dna-cerebellar-development-81b4",
  "summary": "Recent preprints connect DNA repair factors, demethylation and somatic retrotransposition to neuronal gene expression and brain development.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is how DNA maintenance pathways intersect with neural gene regulation and brain development. In human cerebellar organoids, loss of TDP2 reduces PKA-CREB signalling and Purkinje cell maturation, and cAMP activation rescues growth. AAG competes with TDG for oxidized methylcytosine substrates, tuning active DNA demethylation, single-strand break formation and neuronal gene expression. LUSTRE, a single-cell assay, maps L1 insertion sites in about 17,600 adult human neurons to estimate somatic retrotransposition rates. Related preprints address murine SAMHD1 isoforms in replication fork dynamics, transposable element activity in aging visceral adipose tissue, and RepoV-based single-copy enhancer reporters in neural organoids. The new elements are mechanistic links between repair factors and signalling or demethylation, and single-cell resolution of somatic L1 activity in the human brain.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
